WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.723 --> 00:00:05.760
Speaker 1: But I'll tell you, as I said, the&nbsp;
polls are shift and shift and in pretty good ways.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:12.080
Right. And one of the biggest things that we're&nbsp;
seeing happening is that people are flocking away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:17.600
from Donald Trump as a result of this January six,&nbsp;
you know, the televised hearings and everything.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:27.440
And one of the people. Who is watching this&nbsp;
happening and seeing how Republicans are reacting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:34.640
Happens to be Republican pollster Frank Luntz.&nbsp;
Now, Frank Luntz appeared on CNN yesterday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.680
And on CNN, he was actually asked about&nbsp;
an issue I talked about yesterday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:46.640
Ron DeSantis beating Donald Trump in that new New&nbsp;
Hampshire poll. And here is what Mr. Luntz had to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:53.520
say about that. When asked if DeSantis is a threat&nbsp;
to Trump. He said, quote, It's more than a threat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.200
The governor is proving that his approach&nbsp;
and what he's trying to accomplish and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.680
what he has accomplished in Florida is more&nbsp;
significant. And Republicans are now saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:10.720
it's time to move on. There's now polling out that&nbsp;
shows that Donald Trump is actually paying a price&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:21.120
for what these hearings are showing. Now saying&nbsp;
that the Republican Party is ready to move on from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.640
Donald Trump. Based on one poll from University of&nbsp;
New Hampshire with just a few hundred people and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.520
I don't know that I'm willing to say&nbsp;
that, hey, Donald Trump's out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.720
party. Everybody's moving on. That's reading&nbsp;
way too much into a single, way too early poll.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:42.320
However, he's not wrong about the other&nbsp;
polls. Here's one of my favorite things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:49.200
Prior to that very first televised hearing,&nbsp;
two thirds of people in this country&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.760
did not believe that Donald Trump bore&nbsp;
responsibility for what happened on January six.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.520
Today, two thirds of people in this&nbsp;
country believe that Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:04.880
bears responsibility for what happened on&nbsp;
January 6th. It literally flipped. It flipped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:12.880
in two weeks, folks. Two weeks? That's pretty&nbsp;
impressive, right? And that's the point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:19.440
That's how powerful these hearings&nbsp;
are. That's why all of this matters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:24.240
Not just because we want to change&nbsp;
public opinion mostly, obviously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:30.800
because we want justice. We want those&nbsp;
people who broke the law to pay the price.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.640
But I think we're all kidding ourselves if&nbsp;
we don't admit to at least a small degree&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.960
that there is some level of vengeance in us&nbsp;
that feels good about this, that wants it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:46.240
to tank his approval rating, which it has. His&nbsp;
approval rating. Donald Trump's has gone down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:50.560
since these committee hearings began. That is,&nbsp;
of course, what Frank Luntz is referring to.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:57.040
People are tying Donald Trump directly to this.&nbsp;
And as I said, you've got Republican candidates.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:01.600
Dr. Oz is a great one. They're running away from&nbsp;
him, even though Trump came out and backed and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:06.560
made him. You know, had it not been for Trump,&nbsp;
Oz probably wouldn't have won that primary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:14.560
Same thing with J.D. Vance. I don't know if J.D.&nbsp;
Vance is running away from the Trump messaging,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:22.880
but other people are more and more candidates.&nbsp;
And it's not because Donald Trump is still not an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:28.720
influential figure in the party he is, and he will&nbsp;
remain an influential figure in the party whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:35.280
they want him to or not. He's there to stay.&nbsp;
He's your monster. You get to keep him forever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.200
But the voters out there.&nbsp;
They're not so happy with it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:45.440
And we're going to start to see, I promise you,&nbsp;
in the coming weeks, we're going to see more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:51.840
and more Republicans start to run away from&nbsp;
him because, like Luntz said. It's having a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.920
real impact on Donald Trump. It may not be&nbsp;
affecting the rest of the Republican Party,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:01.200
these hearings at least, but if they&nbsp;
continue to try to tie themselves to Trump.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:08.560
It will come back to hurt them in the midterms.&nbsp;
We need to take another quick break. I'm Theron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:13.840
Cousins from Ring of Fire sitting in for David&nbsp;
Pakman. And we'll be right back with more.

